{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Marat</b> — it speaks of the craving soul." "<b>Yitarav</b> — from the matter of <i>'erev rav</i> (a mixed multitude), that is, the heart should be worthy of knowing how to embitter its soul and afflict it with fasting and withhold it from the pleasures of this world, and in its joy, when it rejoices, no alien thing should intermix — and that is grief, which should not intermix in its joy; and that is the joy of the world to come, with which there is no gloom, or the joy of salvation, as in the matter of \"I rejoiced in Your salvation.\""], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:22:43.129415926Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}